# Keeps the build context to what actually ships. Deliberately does NOT exclude
# node_modules: the builder installs its own with `npm ci`, but the image has
# always been built with the host's copy layered on top, and changing how
# dependencies reach production is not something to do quietly alongside an
# unrelated feature.

# The mobile app. Its own node_modules is roughly a gigabyte and none of it is
# served by the web app.
mobile/

# The Android build: keystores, signed bundles, and a second node_modules.
# A keystore in a container image is a keystore one `docker save` from being
# somewhere it cannot be recalled from.
android/

# Local upload volumes. uploads-prod is a copy of real users' photographs.
uploads/
uploads-prod/

# Rebuilt inside the image by `npm run build`.
.next/

.git/
.gitignore
*.log
.env.local
.playwright-mcp/
